WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.689
There is something inherently unnerving about
the sight of someone wearing a gas mask.

00:00:05.689 --> 00:00:10.500
Maybe it’s the wide, soulless portholes
where a person’s eyes should be, or the

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:16.510
huge round filter extruding from their face
that makes them look like something inhuman.

00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:21.110
It could also be the fact that, if ever you
see someone wearing a gas mask, you may be

00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:26.400
surrounded by poisonous gas - and if you’re
not wearing one yourself, someone else’s

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:30.230
gas mask may be the last thing you ever see.

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:35.170
Whatever the reason, you might be wondering
why we’re talking so much about gas masks?

00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:41.579
Well, that’s because you’re about to meet
SCP-1499, which is, as you might have already

00:00:41.579 --> 00:00:44.399
guessed, an anomalous gas mask.

00:00:44.399 --> 00:00:50.940
For all of you military history buffs out
there, SCP-1499 is specifically a Soviet GP-5

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:52.210
gas mask.

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:58.139
These were produced between 1962 and 1990
as a way to protect the wearer from the fallout

00:00:58.139 --> 00:01:00.059
of a nuclear blast.

00:01:00.059 --> 00:01:04.650
Back then, during the Cold War, an atomic
conflict between the United States and the

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:11.079
USSR - that’s Russia - was a constant threat,
and so these masks were sent to most of the

00:01:11.079 --> 00:01:13.369
fallout shelters in the Soviet Union.

00:01:13.369 --> 00:01:18.979
While the GP-5 masks could survive in all
weather and protect against radioactive substances

00:01:18.979 --> 00:01:24.189
for a time, some of their filters contained
a number of harmful chemicals like lead and

00:01:24.189 --> 00:01:25.270
asbestos.

00:01:25.270 --> 00:01:29.710
The fact that these gas masks were airtight
would mean that somebody could end up inhaling

00:01:29.710 --> 00:01:34.189
these toxic chemicals while trying to protect
themselves from nuclear fallout.

00:01:34.189 --> 00:01:38.750
If you look up the definition of “irony”
in the dictionary, you may see a picture of

00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:42.259
one of these gas masks sitting right next
to it.

00:01:42.259 --> 00:01:48.259
And if you think that sounds bad, just wait
until you hear what sets SCP-1499 apart from

00:01:48.259 --> 00:01:49.289
the rest.

00:01:49.289 --> 00:01:54.040
Upon first inspection, the mask seems to still
perform its original function.

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:59.119
The filter works properly and the air-tight
seal is still formed when placed upon somebody’s

00:01:59.119 --> 00:02:00.119
head.

00:02:00.119 --> 00:02:05.429
However, when worn by someone, the anomalous
effects of SCP-1499 will also activate.

00:02:05.429 --> 00:02:09.780
While it doesn’t fuse to the wearer’s
face and turn them into a hysterical zombie

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:15.580
chillingly asking for their mommy, the gas
mask does cause anyone who puts it on to completely

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:16.800
disappear from view.

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:21.830
Now, it is worth noting that this isn’t
a gas mask that grants its user the power

00:02:21.830 --> 00:02:22.830
of invisibility.

00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:28.010
If that was the case, this anomalous item
may actually be desirable.

00:02:28.010 --> 00:02:34.250
SCP-1499 instead causes a person to physically
vanish, as in they are no longer detectable

00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:35.610
at all.

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:41.040
Subjects that have worn SCP-1499 report that
they don’t feel any sensation of moving,

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:46.910
they simply put the mask on and end up…
well, we’ll get to where it is they go.

00:02:46.910 --> 00:02:51.880
You see, through testing, the SCP Foundation’s
researchers were able to determine that giving

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:58.860
someone a two-way radio before they put SCP-1499
on means that they can still be contacted

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:00.480
after they vanish.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:05.580
And it’s through these radios that the Foundation
discovered where the mask wearers go.

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:10.260
During testing, subjects have reportedly found
themselves in a strange, alternate dimension

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:13.390
after putting on SCP-1499.

00:03:13.390 --> 00:03:19.100
It has been described as a dark environment,
inhospitable, barren, and filled with tall,

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:21.410
black tower-like structures.

00:03:21.410 --> 00:03:25.990
You would think being unceremoniously transported
to another dimension by a gas mask would be

00:03:25.990 --> 00:03:27.600
bad enough.

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:30.290
Just wait until you meet the locals.

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:35.140
According to a number of test subjects, a
group of humanoid entities inhabit this dimension.

00:03:35.140 --> 00:03:42.010
Designated as SCP-1499-1, these creatures
are taller than the average person, completely

00:03:42.010 --> 00:03:47.580
nude, and covered from head to toe in a coat
of a dark, viscous substance unlike anything

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:49.660
found in our dimension.

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:56.170
These SCP-1499-1 entities have also been described
as having too many mouths, and a large number

00:03:56.170 --> 00:03:58.730
of eyes covering their bodies.

00:03:58.730 --> 00:04:03.160
From the sound of it, the whole place makes
the Upside Down from Stranger Things sound

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:06.150
like a pleasant destination for a family vacation.

00:04:06.150 --> 00:04:11.500
For the record, the reason we say “according
to a number of test subjects” is that there

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:17.350
has never been any photographic or video evidence
of this place and the creatures that inhabit

00:04:17.350 --> 00:04:18.350
it.

00:04:18.350 --> 00:04:22.019
All that we have gathered to date has come
strictly from first-hand descriptions of those

00:04:22.019 --> 00:04:25.860
experiencing the anomalous effects of SCP-1499.

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:32.030
Luckily, anyone that puts on SCP-1499 and
finds themselves in this place has a very

00:04:32.030 --> 00:04:34.520
quick and easy escape route.

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:39.370
Should a subject encounter any danger in this
dark, inhospitable dimension, then taking

00:04:39.370 --> 00:04:44.330
the gas mask off will drop them right back
into our own plane of existence.

00:04:44.330 --> 00:04:48.340
Upon arriving back, they will not have moved
from the spot they were standing in when they

00:04:48.340 --> 00:04:54.031
first disappeared, but it is unknown exactly
how the gas mask is able to return them, or

00:04:54.031 --> 00:04:57.790
indeed how it can send someone to an entirely
different dimension at all.

00:04:57.790 --> 00:05:02.490
So, a gateway to another dimension, that’s
what the mask is.

00:05:02.490 --> 00:05:08.260
The Foundation has been running tests on SCP-1499
since they first acquired it, at first using

00:05:08.260 --> 00:05:09.670
D Class personnel.

00:05:09.670 --> 00:05:18.150
The first test involving SCP-1499 saw a D
Class, D-67393, told to put on the mask.

00:05:18.150 --> 00:05:22.420
When she did, she found herself transported
inside a building that was constructed from

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:25.290
an unknown black substance.

00:05:25.290 --> 00:05:30.660
D-67393 surveyed the room she was in for a
few seconds, only to hear something moving

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:32.020
close by.

00:05:32.020 --> 00:05:36.980
The sound caused her to panic, and she wrenched
the gas mask off her face, returning to the

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:38.010
test chamber.

00:05:38.010 --> 00:05:42.910
Given that there was now a risk of losing
SCP-1499, the Foundation moved forward with

00:05:42.910 --> 00:05:47.220
tests involving trained agents, instead of
D Class personnel.

00:05:47.220 --> 00:05:51.520
Following this, the next test involved an
“Agent C” putting on the mask, and like

00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:55.900
the D Class before him, he found himself in
the same dark room.

00:05:55.900 --> 00:06:01.450
But instead of taking off SCP-1499 at the
first sound of trouble, this agent explored

00:06:01.450 --> 00:06:02.940
his surroundings.

00:06:02.940 --> 00:06:07.820
Agent C was able to descend the building to
a reasonable degree, until he heard sounds

00:06:07.820 --> 00:06:10.130
coming from the floor below.

00:06:10.130 --> 00:06:17.220
After hiding himself, Agent C witnessed the
very first sighting of the SCP-1499-1 creatures,

00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:22.720
remaining undetected and then safely removing
the mask when the creatures had passed.

00:06:22.720 --> 00:06:29.370
Another agent, known as Agent U, was selected
for an SCP-1499 test, chosen especially for

00:06:29.370 --> 00:06:31.810
her extensive training in stealth.

00:06:31.810 --> 00:06:34.630
Like those before her, she put on the gas
mask.

00:06:34.630 --> 00:06:39.950
Instantly, she found herself in the place
where her predecessor had left off, and continued

00:06:39.950 --> 00:06:42.380
the exploration of the building.

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:46.710
Detecting movement from the floors above,
Agent U exited the building and spotted a

00:06:46.710 --> 00:06:50.570
number of SCP-1499-1 instances.

00:06:50.570 --> 00:06:55.040
The creatures were mulling aimlessly around,
each sporting their own unique mutations,

00:06:55.040 --> 00:06:58.710
occasionally uttering low, grating noises.

00:06:58.710 --> 00:07:03.110
By now, if they were still using D-Classes,
they probably would have lost the mask and

00:07:03.110 --> 00:07:06.100
the people wearing it a hundred times over.

00:07:06.100 --> 00:07:09.600
Never get a D-Class to do a field agent’s
job.

00:07:09.600 --> 00:07:14.280
Making her way past more of the tall, dark
structures, the agent followed and observed

00:07:14.280 --> 00:07:15.880
a group of four creatures.

00:07:15.880 --> 00:07:20.000
A fifth approached them, prompting one from
the group to step forward.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:26.790
As Agent U watched, these SCP-1499 creatures
began violently assaulting each other, until

00:07:26.790 --> 00:07:30.850
she too pulled the gas mask off and returned
to the Foundation.

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:37.290
Shortly afterward, one final agent, Agent
K, was sent into this alternate dimension.

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:42.760
This was less of a test, more a mission with
the purposes of reconnaissance, to give the

00:07:42.760 --> 00:07:47.780
Foundation a better, clearer idea of what
the environment was like, and to possibly

00:07:47.780 --> 00:07:52.890
even make contact with the SCP-1499-1s and
understand them better.

00:07:52.890 --> 00:07:56.810
However, the outcome that followed could not
have been worse.

00:07:56.810 --> 00:08:00.160
Agent K appeared in the other dimension between
two of the black structures.

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:04.660
The lighting made it difficult to see much
of the environment around him, but he remarked

00:08:04.660 --> 00:08:10.240
that the ‘buildings’ resembled tall spires,
constructed out of hard rock, as was the ground

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:11.610
beneath him.

00:08:11.610 --> 00:08:18.280
After a few short minutes, he soon spotted
a group of SCP-1499-1s entering a larger structure,

00:08:18.280 --> 00:08:22.870
an elaborate building with a number of towers
and spikes on it, as well as what appeared

00:08:22.870 --> 00:08:24.310
to be blood.

00:08:24.310 --> 00:08:29.210
Approaching the building with caution, Agent
K located a small, secluded side entrance,

00:08:29.210 --> 00:08:31.630
away from the larger front door.

00:08:31.630 --> 00:08:35.159
As quietly as he could, he made his way inside.

00:08:35.159 --> 00:08:40.389
The sounds of grinding filled the air from
all around him, as Agent K saw a huge group

00:08:40.389 --> 00:08:43.059
of the mutated, humanoid creatures.

00:08:43.059 --> 00:08:49.279
Each one had their mouth wide open, all of
their mouths wide open, making a chorus of

00:08:49.279 --> 00:08:50.899
grating sounds.

00:08:50.899 --> 00:08:56.149
The entities were, according to K’s description,
all facing towards one of the SCP-1499-1s

00:08:56.149 --> 00:09:02.000
that was standing on a platform in front of
them, with a number of bodies around it.

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:07.149
This creature seemed to be leading an odd
ritual and began to cut open its own torso.

00:09:07.149 --> 00:09:11.680
Wormlike creatures spilled out of the open
wound and a beam of light followed, projecting

00:09:11.680 --> 00:09:13.980
out of the entity’s chest.

00:09:13.980 --> 00:09:17.569
Agent K realized that this light was some
form of portal.

00:09:17.569 --> 00:09:21.279
Another worm, like the kind that had come
out of the ritual leader’s chest, began

00:09:21.279 --> 00:09:22.980
to appear in the portal.

00:09:22.980 --> 00:09:27.829
Deciding to act, Agent K dashed out from his
hiding place, opening fire at the creatures

00:09:27.829 --> 00:09:29.180
all around him.

00:09:29.180 --> 00:09:33.300
He reached for something glowing in the lead
entity’s chest, which he thought was bringing

00:09:33.300 --> 00:09:35.410
the worm creature through the portal.

00:09:35.410 --> 00:09:40.290
Grabbing it, Agent K pulled off the gas mask
and found himself back at the Foundation…

00:09:40.290 --> 00:09:42.459
holding a human heart.

00:09:42.459 --> 00:09:43.869
But it doesn’t end there.

00:09:43.869 --> 00:09:49.160
At the exact same time, on the exact same
date, a man attacked the Cathedral of Christ

00:09:49.160 --> 00:09:51.779
the Saviour in Moscow, Russia.

00:09:51.779 --> 00:09:55.869
During the church’s morning services, the
gunman entered dressed in a suit with a gas

00:09:55.869 --> 00:10:00.220
mask over his face, and proceeded to shoot
ten civilians.

00:10:00.220 --> 00:10:04.540
Six were killed, three left in critical condition
including the church’s chanter.

00:10:04.540 --> 00:10:08.449
However, the worst occurred to the priest
performing the service.

00:10:08.449 --> 00:10:12.920
The attacker ran to the front of the cathedral,
producing a knife which he used to cut open

00:10:12.920 --> 00:10:15.529
the priest’s chest and remove his heart.

00:10:15.529 --> 00:10:20.019
Then, just as quickly as he had appeared,
the assailant vanished before the eyes of

00:10:20.019 --> 00:10:25.320
multiple witnesses, and Moscow police were
unable to find any trace of the man.

00:10:25.320 --> 00:10:28.699
Officially, the cathedral was attacked by
Nikolai Orlov.

00:10:28.699 --> 00:10:33.230
Undercover Foundation operatives inside Russia’s
media and military have spread this cover

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:37.379
story of a violent man who acted alone in
his attack on the church.

00:10:37.379 --> 00:10:43.079
Meanwhile, the SCP Foundation is keeping Agent
K detained, questioning him about his involvement

00:10:43.079 --> 00:10:44.529
in the incident.

00:10:44.529 --> 00:10:50.220
According to him, everything happened exactly
as he described it, no church, no priest,

00:10:50.220 --> 00:10:54.910
just him wearing SCP-1499 and surrounded by
the creatures.

00:10:54.910 --> 00:11:00.100
The audio recordings taken from his exploration
mission also seem to align with his story.

00:11:00.100 --> 00:11:04.490
But that still doesn’t explain how another
figure in a gas mask appeared in Moscow and

00:11:04.490 --> 00:11:07.499
claimed the lives of multiple churchgoers.

00:11:07.499 --> 00:11:14.459
Not only that, but dispatching them in the
exact same way Agent K dealt with the SCP-1499-1

00:11:14.459 --> 00:11:16.129
creatures.

00:11:16.129 --> 00:11:21.829
The only possible explanation was that Agent
K was the perpetrator, even if - in his mind

00:11:21.829 --> 00:11:24.360
- he was still telling the truth.

00:11:24.360 --> 00:11:31.220
Hoping to avoid another incident, the O5 Council
has suspended all further testing with SCP-1499.

00:11:31.220 --> 00:11:35.800
Agent K has been scheduled to undergo a psychological
evaluation, believing the creature he saw

00:11:35.800 --> 00:11:39.129
being summoned had to be stopped at all costs.

00:11:39.129 --> 00:11:43.580
The other agents and the D Class involved
in earlier testing are all being brought in

00:11:43.580 --> 00:11:45.189
for questioning as well.

00:11:45.189 --> 00:11:50.279
It is still unknown what the anomalous effect
of SCP-1499 truly is.

00:11:50.279 --> 00:11:53.529
Is it actually capable of transporting someone
to another dimension?

00:11:53.529 --> 00:11:58.589
Or does it give a person hallucinations, that
make them think they’re galavanting off

00:11:58.589 --> 00:12:04.939
in dimension X, while they’re actually walking
up to a church about to do something unthinkable?

00:12:04.939 --> 00:12:07.709
With testing suspended, we may never know.

00:12:07.709 --> 00:12:13.430
But it leaves us with an important message:
Think carefully about everything you do, because

00:12:13.430 --> 00:12:18.170
what you think you can see doesn’t always
reflect what’s really there...

00:12:18.170 --> 00:12:25.769
Now go check out “Robot Battle Royale SCP-1370
- Pesterbot” and “SCP-261 - Pan-Dimensional

00:12:25.769 --> 00:12:30.579
Vending Machine” for more fascinating anomalous
objects from the SCP Foundation!

